> *"The reports of my death have been greatly exaggerated - but so, sometimes, have the reports of my inevitable victory. A movement is not a single election; it is the work of organizing people to build power together, over years, against everything arrayed to stop them."*

 - fictional epigraph, in the spirit of democratic-socialist organizing literature of the period

This is a game of alternate history. While plausibility is a major concern, keep in mind that this is a *game*, and that any divergence from actual events will necessarily involve some element of make-believe. Real political parties and institutions are referenced factually; specific advisors, rivals, and rank-and-file characters are fictionalized composites rather than real people. Please let the author know if there are any glaring mistakes.

For more information on the structure of American government and the Seventh Party System, see the "Library" page on the top left. If this is your first time playing the game, it is strongly recommended that you read at least some of this information.

