@2015_main
new-page: true
go-to: main if difficulty >= 0; main.main_easy if difficulty < 0

= 2015

It is the tenth year since the financial crisis, and the recovery has been long, uneven, and deeply unequal. A generation that came of age during the crash carries record student debt into a job market of stagnant wages. Something is stirring on the American left for the first time in decades: a small, once-dormant socialist organization is growing again, and an independent senator from Vermont is weighing a most unlikely campaign.

Now, the task ahead is to turn this stirring into organized power - within a Democratic Party that does not yet know what has arrived at its door, and against a Republican Party where an insurgency of its own is about to erupt.


